    "durationMs": 292296,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Setup** — Created a Laravel 11 project with Composer (scaffolded in /tmp, moved into /workspace around the existing .git), dependencies installed.\n\n**Code** — `routes/api.php` registered with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php`; a `links` migration (unique case-sensitive `code` via `ascii_bin` collation, text `url`, `clicks` counter); an Eloquent `Link` model; and a `LinkController` with manual validation producing `{\"error\": ...}` on 409/404/422, URL validation requiring an absolute http/https URL with a host via `parse_url`, code rule `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`, collision-safe random code generation, and an atomic SQL `increment` for clicks.\n\n**Config** — Stripped all `DB_*` lines from `.env` so the provided environment variables are the sole database source; `start.sh` applies migrations (with a short retry for DB startup races) then runs `php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground; README has a \"Starting the server\" section.\n\n**Verification** — A 40-check HTTP battery passed (39 functional PASS; the single reported \"FAIL\" was whitespace in my own assertion — all 80 burst requests returned 200, confirming no throttling). Covered: 201 responses with unchanged URLs and `clicks: 0`, duplicate code 409, all 422 validation cases including malformed JSON, exact 302 Location headers, clicks incrementing exactly once per redirect and never via `GET /links/{code}`, ascending list order, case-sensitive codes, and click counts plus links surviving a full server restart. Server was stopped afterward and the database left in a clean, freshly-migrated state with an empty `links` table."
